implementationPlan.description:
docs/MCP_SERVER.md, edit the moe.get_commit_scope section only (around line 662). Five live tasks declare this file and the checkout already carries a peer's uncommitted hunks (get_context isEpicFinal / epic finalTaskId, update_epic). Never revert, reflow or tidy anything outside this section. (1) Returns: add assigneeProtected: boolean right after assigneeAlive, with a comment covering these points:
- false for an unassigned task;
- true while the assignee's worker record exists and is not DEAD (however stale its lastActivityAt), or while the task has a non-closed attempt that this assignee opened;
- malformed records fail closed;
- the value is caller-independent and the field is additive.
Annotate assigneeAlive as the 120 s display-presence window (isWorkerAlive): it is never evidence that the assignee is dead and never permission to land. (2) Notes: add a 'Live-assignee protection' bullet covering:
- the field is what a landing session that is not the assignee consults before it lands the task's source paths (wrapper side: task-6aa460bb33184e1b84fc9c9e5c0a4560);
- while it is true, that session lands no source path for the task;
- only boolean false permits a landing, so a missing field (older daemon), a non-boolean value or a failed RPC must be treated as protected, never coerced to false;
- the disk fallback has no protection signal, so a wrapper on it cannot infer that a foreign assignee is dead.
(3) Keep the 'No ownership guard' bullet true (the tool still serves every caller and refuses none) and the fallback bullet accurate. Re-read the section against the code and tests; every statement must hold. Nothing else in the file changes.
